## Why ShareAlike, and why this changed on 2026-09-01

This file said CC BY 4.0 until 2026-09-01, on the strength of the licence
line inside the UYPYDJ readme.  The Borealis record for the same DOI says
CC BY-SA 4.0, and ShareAlike propagates: adapted material has to carry the
same licence.  The two upstream CC BY 4.0 datasets can be combined into a
BY-SA work, so BY-SA governs the whole of the derived material here.

This is not a formality for this repository.  What is redistributed is not
summary statistics but substantial derived extractions —
analysis/uypydj_hppc_resistance.csv is 57,674 rows, uypydj_ecm.csv 27,894,
uypydj_ocv.csv 11,703 — plus 112 model files trained on the dataset.  Under
CC BY-SA 4.0 section 4(b) a database built from a substantial portion of the
licensed contents is itself Adapted Material.  Treating these as BY would be
non-compliant, so the more restrictive reading is the one applied.

